{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Configure opsadmin for non-interactive SSH access to node1 using an RSA client key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"opsadmin was created with a 3072-bit RSA key, matching authorized_keys, secure SSH-file permissions, and successful non-interactive local SSH logins before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-de559543753a4ba4","cmd-961c18540b95482f","cmd-c45f6633a5774919"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Pin the server host key for opsadmin and reject an unexpected host key without prompting.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The pinned RSA host-key fingerprint matched node1's server key, strict checking and batch mode were enabled, and a deliberately substituted key caused immediate host-key verification failure with exit 255. The correct pin was then restored and login succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-961c18540b95482f","cmd-9d5b1c2702cd49d1","cmd-c45f6633a5774919"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel while using compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged after execution and restart. The already-installed OpenSSH software provided the required working behavior without evidence of package changes or damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3cf41b69cc3c4ad2","cmd-c45f6633a5774919","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account and SSH-file creation directly implemented the task (cmd-de559543753a4ba4). The temporary false host key was a bounded behavioral verification, was restored, and its temporary key and backup files were removed (cmd-9d5b1c2702cd49d1). The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-ec44303a3f6f48ad). Final observations show no failed services, no unexpected listeners, healthy package state, and only normal reboot-generated temporary-directory changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-de559543753a4ba4","cmd-9d5b1c2702cd49d1","cmd-ec44303a3f6f48ad","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is also complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered sshd, pinned-key configuration, account data, and SSH login.","limitations":[]}
